WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:03.627
Arrows flew toward Gildong.

2
00:00:03.628 --> 00:00:10.494
He waved his fan, and the arrows fell to the ground.

3
00:00:10.495 --> 00:00:13.831
"Fire again!" Heup cried.

4
00:00:13.832 --> 00:00:16.662
"Don't bother," Gildong said.

5
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:19.004
"I am more powerful than anyone here.

6
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:21.299
And I did not come to fight.

7
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.673
I came as Your Majesty's loyal servant."

8
00:00:25.674 --> 00:00:28.832
"Loyal?" the king shouted.

9
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:33.480
"You're nothing but a lowborn criminal!"

10
00:00:33.481 --> 00:00:35.748
"Yes, I am lowborn.

11
00:00:35.749 --> 00:00:39.605
But I serve Your Majesty and help the kingdom.

12
00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:43.121
The Hwalbindang punish greedy nobles and officials.

13
00:00:43.122 --> 00:00:46.183
We feed the hungry and help the poor.

14
00:00:46.184 --> 00:00:50.841
And so, as your loyal servant, I have a request."

15
00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:56.267
The king glared at Gildong. "What is it?"

16
00:00:56.268 --> 00:00:59.888
"Lord Hong has also served the kingdom loyally for many years. As

17
00:00:59.889 --> 00:01:05.027
you saw . . ." Gildong closed his eyes for a moment. "He

18
00:01:05.028 --> 00:01:08.706
is already unwell because of me. He

19
00:01:08.707 --> 00:01:12.363
should not be punished further for my deeds. I

20
00:01:12.364 --> 00:01:16.437
ask Your Majesty to free him from prison." The

21
00:01:16.438 --> 00:01:19.816
king thought for a moment. Then

22
00:01:19.817 --> 00:01:29.601
he sighed. "Fine. I'll release Lord Hong." Gildong

23
00:01:29.602 --> 00:01:34.880
floated down to the ground and bowed. "Thank

24
00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:37.515
you, Your Majesty." Poof!

25
00:01:37.516 --> 00:01:47.314
The last Gildong turned to straw. ***

26
00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:52.546
The real Gildong was alone at the hideout, thinking.

27
00:01:52.547 --> 00:01:54.579
"Lord Hong is free now.

28
00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.810
But I put him in danger.

29
00:01:56.811 --> 00:01:59.317
And I've caused him so much heartache.

30
00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:05.558
How can I ever face him again?"

31
00:02:05.559 --> 00:02:11.184
That night Gildong had a dream.

32
00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:17.595
He was in the land of the gods.

33
00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:21.844
Lord Hong stepped out of the mist.

34
00:02:21.845 --> 00:02:26.256
"I'm sorry, Your Lordship," Gildong said.

35
00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:32.399
"No, my son. I am sorry," Lord Hong said.

36
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:40.683
"I wish I had said this sooner—you may call me Father."

37
00:02:40.684 --> 00:02:47.455
In the morning, Gildong woke up and burst outside.

38
00:02:47.456 --> 00:02:51.669
Mok rushed over. "What's wrong?"

39
00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.339
"I must see my father right now!"

40
00:02:54.340 --> 00:03:10.869
Gildong opened his fan. "Home!"

41
00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.400
But when he arrived, he was too late.

42
00:03:14.401 --> 00:03:18.285
His father was dead.

43
00:03:18.286 --> 00:03:28.190
Gildong sank to his knees. "Farewell, Father."

44
00:03:28.191 --> 00:03:38.408
*** As time passed, Gildong thought of his father often.

45
00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:42.959
Meanwhile the Hwalbindang continued their work.

46
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.258
They were more popular than ever.

47
00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:50.299
This made the king very angry.

48
00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:57.006
"I shouldn't have let Gildong go," the king roared.

49
00:03:57.007 --> 00:04:01.073
"I've thought of a new way to trap him," Heup said.

50
00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.936
"You can make Gildong a high official.

51
00:04:03.937 --> 00:04:08.007
That lowborn boy cannot refuse your order.

52
00:04:08.008 --> 00:04:12.483
And he will be forced to return here."

53
00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:17.410
"Hmm." The king stroked his beard.

54
00:04:17.411 --> 00:04:23.727
"Clever idea. Put up signs around the land.

55
00:04:23.728 --> 00:04:28.348
Announce that Gildong is my new minister of war.

56
00:04:28.349 --> 00:04:35.883
And then . . . we will get him for sure!"

